<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-bs-theme="dark">

<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  {% include "seo_head.html.j2" %}
  <link href="/static/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
</head>

<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>About this Nitter status page</h1>
    <p><a href="/">Home</a></p>
    <p id="update-interval">Uptime check interval: {{uptime_interval_s}}s.</p>
    <p>Instance re-fetching interval, including RSS & version check: {{wiki_interval_s}}s.</p>
    <p>Fetched latest commit: {{latest_commit}}</p>

    <p>The following paths are checked per instance:</p>
    <ul>
      {%- for path in checked_paths %}
      <li><code>{{path}}</code></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    <p>Instance owners can login at <a href="/admin">/admin</a> for settings and more information.</p>

    <h4>Table Explanations</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><code>Country</code> for the host country reported in the instance wiki.</li>
      <li><code>Healthy</code> stands for hosts which are reachable and pass a content check.<br>
        Known bad hosts are marked with a ❓. These instances prevent healthchecks (for example through long caching).
      </li>
      <li><code>Average Time</code> is the response time average over the last {{ping_avg_interval_h}} hours. This is
        not a network ping and can be influenced by caching and twitter servers.</li>
      <li><code>All Time %</code> for all time percentage of the instance being healthy.</li>
      <li><code>RSS</code> whether the host has RSS feeds enabled. Instances might have a whitelist.</li>
      <li><code>LSH</code> Last Seen Healthy, for the last time an instance was seen healthy.</li>
      <li><code>Nitter Version</code> which nitter version the host reports.</li>
      <li><code>Connectivity</code> the IP connectivity support. One of <code>All</code>, <code>IPv4</code>,
        <code>IPv6</code>
      </li>
      <li><code>Points</code> is a weighted instance score based on
        <ul>
          <li>the availability over the last 3h</li>
          <li>30 days</li>
          <li>120 days</li>
          <li>reported nitter version</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ul>

    <p>Settings for visible columns are stored locally per client.</p>

    <h4>API</h4>
    <p id="api">
      The same data as visible in the website/table can also be fetched as JSON from <code>/api/v1/instances</code> (<a
        rel="nofollow" href="/api/v1/instances">link</a>).
      Note that the data only changes in the intervals stated <a href="#update-interval">above</a>. Thus requesting it
      very often will get you rate limited.
    </p>
    <p>
      Scraping is allowed on
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://nitter.cf/">nitter.cf</a>,
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://nitter.gq/">nitter.gq</a>,
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://xitter.cf/">xitter.cf</a>,
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://xitter.gq/">xitter.gq</a>,
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://teapaw.org/">teapaw.org</a>,
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://teapawt.net/">teapawt.net</a>, and
      <a rel="nofollow external" href="https://teapawt.org/">teapawt.org</a>.
      Ask the operator for permission before scraping any other Nitter instance.
    </p>
    <p>The JSON API is for reading this status page. It refreshes on the interval above, so requesting it very often gets rate limited.</p>

    <p>Agent notes: <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>. Sitemap: <a href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap.xml</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/4cuck/nitter-status">Source</a> (AGPL-3.0-only).</p>
    <p>License: AGPL3</p>
  </div>
</body>

</html>
